# Security

Security-sensitive work must preserve:
- backend authorization and cross-tenant isolation;
- parent/child ownership validation;
- explicit permission vs entitlement checks;
- CSRF/session protections;
- server-side input validation;
- safe secret storage/masking/logging;
- XSS protection for raw/rich HTML;
- SSRF protection for customer-configured outbound URLs;
- safe upload MIME/size/path handling;
- no Draft/private data leaking into public output.

Add focused regression tests for a discovered security defect.

## Review trigger

Use ONE independent Security review after implementation when the task changes auth, tenancy, permissions, secrets, public endpoints, uploads, outbound HTTP, publishing, domains, exports/personal data or extension runtime.

Do not also launch QA + Reviewer + UI Reviewer automatically unless their own triggers apply.
